'' A 'using' offers a 'Word' function, and windows.bi (read for sys/win's import) declares
'' type WORD. The program's own bare WORD would be TKO0919; but BGR( ) is windows.bi's macro,
'' and the WORD its expansion casts to is written in windows.bi, against windows.bi's own
'' declaration -- not ambiguous.
#import "sys/win"
namespace shades
    function Word( ) as integer
        return 1
    end function
end namespace
using shades
print hex( BGR( 1, 2, 3 ) )
